{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-hos-5-1","title":"Hosea 5:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The judgments of God are denounced against the priests, people, and princes, both of Israel and Judah, for their manifold sins. 15 An intimation is given of mercy on their repentance.</p>\n<p>O priests. 4:1,6,7; 6:9; Mal 1:6; 2:1 O house. 7:3-5; 1Ki 14:7-16; 21:18-22; 2Ch 21:12-15; Jer 13:18; 22:1-9 Am 7:9; Mic 3:1,9 for. 9:11-17; 10:15; 13:8 ye have. 9:8; Mic 7:2; Hab 1:15-17 Tabor. Jud 4:6; Jer 46:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-2","title":"Hosea 5:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the revolters. 6:9; 9:15; Jer 6:28 profound. Ps 64:3-6; 140:1-5; Isa 29:15; Jer 11:18,19; 18:18; Lu 22:2-5 Ac 23:12-15 though. or, and, etc. a rebuker. Heb. a correction. 6:5; Isa 1:5; Jer 5:3; 25:3-7; Am 4:6-12; Zep 3:1,2; Re 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-3","title":"Hosea 5:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>know. Am 3:2; Heb 4:13; Re 3:15 Ephraim. 9,11,13; 6:4; 8:11; 12:1; 13:1; Ge 48:19,20; De 33:17; Isa 7:5,8,9,17 thou. 4:17,18; 1Ki 12:26-33; 14:14-16; Eze 23:5-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-4","title":"Hosea 5:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>They will not frame their doings. Heb. They will not give.Or, their doings will not suffer them. Ps 36:1-4; 78:8; Joh 3:19,20; 2Th 2:11,12 for. 4:12; Jer 50:38 and. 4:1; 1Sa 2:12; Ps 9:10; Jer 9:6,24; 22:15,16; 24:7; Joh 8:55; 16:3 1Jo 2:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-5","title":"Hosea 5:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>the pride. 7:10; Pr 30:13; Isa 3:9; 9:9,10; 28:1-3 testify. Isa 44:9; 59:12; Jer 14:7; Mt 23:31; Lu 19:22 fall in. 4:5; 14:1; Pr 11:5,21; 14:32; 24:16; Am 5:2 Judah. 14; 8:14; 2Ki 17:19,20; Eze 23:31-35; Am 2:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-6","title":"Hosea 5:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>go. Ex 10:9,24-26; Pr 15:8; 21:27; Jer 7:4; Mic 6:6,7 they. Pr 1:28; Isa 1:11-15; 66:3; Jer 11:11; La 3:44; Eze 8:18; Am 5:21-23 Mic 3:4; Joh 7:34 he. So 5:6; Lu 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-7","title":"Hosea 5:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>dealt. 6:7; Isa 48:8; 59:13; Jer 3:20; 5:11 begotten. Ne 13:23,24; Ps 144:7,11; Mal 2:11-15 a month. Eze 12:28; Zec 11:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-8","title":"Hosea 5:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Blow. 8:1; Jer 4:5; 6:1; Joe 2:1,15 Gibeah. 9:9; 10:9; Jud 19:12-15; 20:4-6; 1Sa 15:34; 2Sa 21:6; Isa 10:29 Ramah. 1Sa 7:17; 8:4; 15:34 Beth-aven. 4:15; 10:5,8; Jos 7:2; 1Ki 12:29 after. Jud 5:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-9","title":"Hosea 5:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Ephraim. 12,14; 8:8; 9:11-17; 11:5,6; 13:1-3,15,16; Job 12:14; Isa 28:1-4 Am 3:14,15; 7:9,17 have. Isa 46:10; 48:3,5; Am 3:7; Zec 1:6; Joh 16:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-10","title":"Hosea 5:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>princes. 5 remove. De 19:14; 27:17; 2Ki 16:7-9; 2Ch 28:16-22; Pr 17:14; 22:28 like. Ps 32:6; 88:17; 93:3,4; Mt 7:27; Lu 6:49</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-11","title":"Hosea 5:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>oppressed. De 28:33; 2Ki 15:16-20,29; Am 5:11,12 he willingly. 1Ki 12:26-33; Mic 6:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-12","title":"Hosea 5:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>as a. Job 13:28; Isa 50:9; 51:8 as. Pr 12:4 rottenness. or, a worm. Jon 4:7; Mr 9:44-48</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-13","title":"Hosea 5:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>his wound. Jer 30:12,14; Mic 1:9 went. 7:11; 10:6; 12:1; 2Ki 15:19,29; 16:7; 2Ch 28:16-18 to king Jareb. or, to the king of Jareb; or, to the king thatshould plead. yet. 2Ch 28:20,21; Jer 30:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-14","title":"Hosea 5:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>as a lion. 13:7,8; Job 10:16; Ps 7:2; La 3:10; Am 3:4-8 will tear. Ps 7:2; 50:22; Mic 5:8 none. De 28:31; Job 10:7; Isa 5:29; Am 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hos-5-15","title":"Hosea 5:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HOS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>return. 6; Ex 25:21,22; 1Ki 8:10-13; Ps 132:14; Isa 26:21; Eze 8:6; 10:4 Eze 11:23; Mic 1:3 till. 14:1-3; Le 26:40-42; De 4:29-31; 30:1-3; 1Ki 8:47,48; 2Ch 6:36,37 2Ch 7:14; Ne 1:8,9; Job 33:27; Isa 64:5-9; Jer 3:13; 29:12-14 Jer 31:18-20; Eze 6:9; 20:43; 36:31; Da 9:4-12 acknowledge their offence. Heb. be guilty. in their. Jud 4:3; 6:6,7; 10:10-16; 2Ch 33:12,13; Job 27:8-10; Ps 50:15; 78:34 Ps 83:16; Pr 1:27,28; 8:17; Isa 26:9,16; Jer 2:27; Zep 2:1-3 Lu 13:25</p>"}]}